2026-05-26T12:24:31.294Z {"session_id":"8e6f4227-1c72-4eb5-85c7-a4a0703b9a66","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\8e6f4227-1c72-4eb5-85c7-a4a0703b9a66.jsonl","cwd":"E:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"286/286. Here's the root cause and what changed:\n\n**Root cause**: `shutil.rmtree(\"./data/lightrag\", ignore_errors=True)` silently swallows the wipe failure. On Windows, if any coroutine (e.g., a concurrent chat search) holds a file handle open inside `data/lightrag/`, the OS blocks deletion. With `ignore_errors=True`, `reinitialize()` doesn't know the wipe failed — it creates a fresh `LightRAG` object but `initialize_storages()` loads the **old** `kv_store_doc_status.json` containing 162 failed entries from the previous run. LightRAG then treats every re-inserted chunk as a duplicate and skips entity extraction entirely. The UI still says \"16 docs done\" because the router just counts files it attempted, not whether LightRAG actually processed them.\n\n**The fix** in `reinitialize()` ([lightrag_service.py:171](app/services/lightrag_service.py#L171)):\n1. Calls `rag.finalize_storages()` first to release open file handles before the wipe (wrapped in try/except in case the LightRAG version doesn't expose this)\n2. Drops `ignore_errors=True` so a wipe failure raises a `RuntimeError` instead of silently continuing\n3. The error propagates up through the SSE stream's outer `try/except` → user sees `{\"status\": \"error\"}` + `{\"status\": \"done\"}` instead of a phantom \"all 16 done\" success","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}

